 "intro": {
  "title": "TUNING FORK FIELDS",
  "lines": [
   "Every row on this hill is a fork, and every fork has been tuned.",
   "What gets struck here is paid for somewhere else."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Next: the Reliquary Road, where the Vael keep the people they have finished with.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [5, 58],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Terraces, and on every terrace a row of standing forks, brass and green, taller than a man. They are all humming, so low I feel it in my hands before I hear it."
  },
  {
   "id": "fork",
   "at": [9, 51],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A fork rings at a shot, answers its neighbours down the row, and everything asleep near them wakes. The arc lamp and a blow are heard from least far."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate",
   "at": [15, 45],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "FORK PLATE",
   "text": "A brass plate hammered onto the foot, in our letters: AMBLER, T. BOSUN. Somebody here had that courtesy. I count eight more plates in this row."
  },
  {
   "id": "tend",
   "at": [30, 44],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "They are tending the forks. Weeding round them, wiping them down, putting an ear to them. Nobody looks up. I would like to keep it that way."
  },
  {
   "id": "stair",
   "at": [24, 43],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The lower flight of the great stair has come down, and the gate at its head is shut. The harvesters go up through the barn and its hay loft."
  },
  {
   "id": "count",
   "at": [50, 46],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: a long number, a longer number, then one short note that rises like a question. Struck and owed, if I had to guess."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [58, 47],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The east wall of this barn rings hollow behind the crates."
  },
  {
   "id": "gate",
   "at": [24, 36],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The gate at the head of the stair is chained shut. The chain runs west along the terrace, into the winch house at the end of it.",
   "unless": [
    "msg:winch"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "split",
   "at": [6, 34],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The back wall of the winch house is split from floor to roof, and cold air comes through the split. One good shot would open it."
  },
  {
   "id": "shelf",
   "at": [6, 29],
   "radius": 1.5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A forkwright's cupboard. Shells for the scattergun that burn, and a brass plate with nothing stamped on it yet."
  },
  {
   "id": "winch",
   "at": [0, 0],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The chain runs out along the terrace and the stair gate swings open. Something on the field above it has started walking."
  },
  {
   "id": "tower",
   "at": [40, 23],
   "radius": 3.5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A round tower on the top of the hill with a bell inside it the size of a boat. Everything on this hill is tuned to that."
  },
  {
   "id": "lever",
   "at": [43, 10],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A lever on the bell stand. It works the gate in the north wall; the Keepers ring the bell and the gate answers."
  },
  {
   "id": "tune",
   "at": [0, 0],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The gate in the north wall opens. Down the hill, every fork in every field gives one low note, and stops."
  }
 ],
